  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 7.0.451\n\nFix: 32-bit processes using TcAmsServer.dll (PInvoke channel) terminated with an access violation when an AMS port was disconnected, e.g. when an AdsClient was disposed, #351635\n\nVersion 7.0.421\n\nFix: AdsClient/AdsServer connect no longer fails with ClientSyncTimeOut (ConnectPortFailed) on heavily loaded hosts. The router command timeout was raised from 200 ms to 5 s and is configurable per instance via 'AmsRouter:CommandTimeout' (AmsChannelSettings.CommandTimeout). The loopback connection is closed after a timeout.\n\nVersion 7.0.410\n\nFix: Corrected the native AmsConnectEx call so the AMS port name is registered correctly at the router, #337462\n\nFix: An IConfiguration passed to AdsClient, AdsServer or AdsSymbolicServer now configures the AMS router loopback endpoint, channel port type and channel protocol for that instance only, instead of overwriting the process wide AmsConfiguration. Several clients and servers can therefore use different router endpoints within one process, #338067\n\nFix: A configured AmsRouter:LoopbackPort no longer discards the preset loopback address, and vice versa, #338067\n\nFix: The LoopbackNotRegisteredException of a server now reports the endpoint that server actually used instead of the process wide one, #338067\n\nVersion 7.0.307\n\nFix: The server no longer depends on Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder for reading the AmsRouter settings.\n\nVersion 7.0.294\n\nFix: Removed sporadic latency outliers between an ADS request and its AdsServer response, especially on systems with few cores.\n\nEnh: AdsServer allocates significantly less per frame, which reduces GC pressure and Gen2 collections.\n\nFix: Exceptions escaping an AdsServer indication handler are logged instead of being lost, and oversized AMS frames are rejected instead of being allocated.\n\nVersion 7.0.152\n\nEnh: AdsClient.Connect() fails after a timeout instead of hanging when the AMS router doesn't answer\n\nBreakingChange: AdsServer.ConnectServerAsync(CancellationToken cancel) implementation as the async counterpart of AdsServer.ConnectServer (Replaces old obsolete AdsServer.ConnectServerAsync)\n\nVersion 7.0.127\n\nFix: SemaphoreFullException in AsyncLock class, #280297\n\nVersion 7.0.109\n\nEnh: Fewer memory allocations and copy operations for better performance\n\nVersion 7.0.36\n\nBreakingChange: Removed the net6.0 target (.NET 6 is out of support)\n\nVersion 7.0\n\nEnh: Supports locally installed TwinCAT 2 (via PInvoke channel). The fallback to 'TcAmsServer.dll' also enables systems without an open TCP loopback port (e.g. TC2 or TCP loopback disabled), #230847\n\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets, TCP/IP Loopback and PInvoke\n\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
